  <h2>Reflect: what job does the form perform?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">I choose used to when...</span> <span class="ex">Habitual would needs...</span> <span class="ex">Past Simple can describe both...</span> <span class="ex">A state differs from a repeated event because...</span> <span class="ex">Be used to means...</span> <span class="ex">Get used to means...</span></p>
    <p>Create two accurate versions of one routine: a neutral Past Simple report and a memory-style <span class="ex">would</span> version with a clear past frame. Then explain the discourse difference.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the three-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>

